MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The outdoor Gorilla tape feels like a natural next choice because I have bought Gorilla tape before, and weather resistance gives it a clear use for exposed repairs.",
    "The solder-seal connectors and assorted heat-shrink tubing complement my earlier crimp terminals by helping seal and insulate wire repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The large red tubing is related to electrical repair, but I have no identified connection that needs that diameter; an assortment is more useful when the required sizes vary.",
    "Cutting wheels, precision blocks, and a temperature controller assume equipment or projects my purchases do not establish. The test kit and bulk trash bags also lack a clear current need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying maintenance supplies seems to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop tool, even when its specific purpose does not connect to my repairs.",
    "A broad connection to electrical work seems to count too much when the size and practical use of a particular item remain uncertain."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Gorilla tape purchases give me a concrete reason to consider a related tape with a useful added capability.",
    "I choose supplies when I can see how they fit a repair; compatibility, useful sizes, and a clear role alongside what I already have matter more than general usefulness."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in practical repair supplies but stretched it into specialized tools and unrelated needs without enough evidence."
}
